
# Dismiss — close an open overlay on Escape or an outside click. Built on the `listen-document` dom primitive. Call
# `arm-dismiss` with the overlay's disclosure controller when it opens; Escape closes it, and a document click closes
# it too (the headless contract: the panel stops propagation on its own clicks, so only OUTSIDE clicks reach the
# document handler). Reused by popover, dialog, dropdown-menu, context-menu, hover-card, select, sheet, drawer. The
# behavior core for dismissal.

load @term/site/view/reactive
  find signal
  find on-cleanup
load @term/site/dom/dom
  find listen-document
  find listen-key
load ./disclosure
  find close-disclosure

# arm Escape + outside-click dismissal for a disclosure controller. Each listener returns a remover, which is
# registered for cleanup on the surrounding scope, so when the overlay's owner is disposed (the panel unmounts) the
# global handlers detach. No leak. Escape comes through `listen-key`, which every host implements (a hardware keyboard
# on the platform toolkits, the terminal's own keys); it read the browser's KeyboardEvent until 2026-10-03, so no
# overlay closed on Escape anywhere but a browser (swiftui-target-0003)
task arm-dismiss
  take control, like signal
  save drop-key
    call listen-key
      task on-key
        take key, like text
        fork test
          hook test
            call is-equal
              read key
              text <Escape>
          hook hold
            call close-disclosure
              bind self, read control
  call on-cleanup
    read drop-key
  save drop-click
    call listen-document
      text <click>
      task on-click
        take event
        call close-disclosure
          bind self, read control
  call on-cleanup
    read drop-click
